2. NON-COMMERCIAL (NC) — STRICT & UNAMBIGUOUS DEFINITION:
   You may NOT use this material for commercial purposes under any circumstances.
   "Commercial purposes" explicitly includes, but is not limited to:
     a) Use within or on behalf of any company, business, startup, enterprise, firm,
        or for-profit entity.
     b) Deployment across any corporate, workplace, employee, or contractor machines.
     c) Reselling, sublicensing, packaging, charging fees for, or generating revenue
        directly or indirectly from this software or any derivative works.
     d) Using this architecture or its modules as part of paid IT/DevOps consulting,
        contracting, commercial support, or proprietary internal platform tooling.

   Personal, educational, hobbyist, and non-profit home-lab use is 100% permitted.
   Commercial usage requires an explicit, separate written commercial license agreement
   from the author ("nixx").

3. SHARE-ALIKE (SA):
   If you remix, transform, modify, or build upon this software, architecture, or
   configuration, you MUST distribute your contributions under the EXACT SAME license
   (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0). You may not apply legal terms, restrictive licenses, or
   technological DRM measures that legally restrict others from doing anything this
   license permits. All derivative works must preserve full attribution to the original author.

4. MEDIA & CONTENT CREATION CLARIFICATION:
   Creating public tutorials, blog posts, reviews, or videos discussing or showcasing
   this repository (including on ad-supported platforms such as YouTube) is fully
   permitted, provided that:
     a) Prominent credit to "nixx" is included on-screen or in the description.
     b) A direct link to https://github.com/nixxgh/nixosconfig is provided.
     c) The code/configuration itself is not placed behind a paywall.

================================================================================
ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS & UPSTREAM CREDITS
================================================================================

This project stands on the shoulders of giants. The architectural composition,
multi-tenant fleet taxonomy, and blast-radius rebuild pipelines created in this
repository would not have been possible without the foundational technologies
created and maintained by the following five authors, organizations, and teams:

1. Eelco Dolstra & the NixOS / Nixpkgs Contributors
   • Technology : Nix Package Manager, NixOS, and Nixpkgs
   • License    : MIT License
   • Impact     : Provided the pure functional package management and declarative
                  operating system core that makes reproducible infrastructure possible.

2. Robert Helgesson (rycee) & the Home Manager Team (nix-community)
   • Technology : Home Manager (github.com/nix-community/home-manager)
   • License    : MIT License
   • Impact     : Provided the unprivileged user-space and dotfile management framework
                  that powers our standalone user capsules.

3. Hercules CI & Robert Hensing
   • Technology : flake-parts (github.com/hercules-ci/flake-parts)
   • License    : MIT License
   • Impact     : Provided the modular flake architecture and system abstraction
                  layer that allows clean separation of concerns across our fleet.

4. BirdeeHub
   • Technology : nix-wrapper-modules (github.com/BirdeeHub/nix-wrapper-modules)
   • License    : MIT License
   • Impact     : Provided the declarative CLI wrapper system that powers our seamless
                  compositor and terminal runtime bindings.

5. Victor Borja (vic)
   • Technology : import-tree (github.com/vic/import-tree)
   • License    : Apache License 2.0
   • Impact     : Provided the zero-touch recursive filesystem module crawler that
                  eliminates manual boilerplate and dynamically auto-loads our fleet.

We express our deepest gratitude to these upstream creators for making their core
engines freely available under permissive open-source licenses.

